WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.100
-I saw a new report that says
that people should not rake

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.834
all the leaves out of their yard

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.868
because it's actually better
for your lawn's health.

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.100
So, I think, with that in mind,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.300
it's time to say goodbye
to my rake.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.133
Rake, are you there?

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:15.334
-A lifetime of autumns together

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:19.033
and this is how I find out
I'm fired.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.767
-Come on, rake,
don't think of it as fired.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.200
Think of it as retiring.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.367
You can now
do anything you want.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.300
-Man, I want to rake leaves.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.167
Fall is my whole personality.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.501
-Look, your future
is what you make it.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:34.567
We'll see you in the spring,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.300
when it's time
to clear the flower beds.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.667
-You're right, Jimmy.

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.934
Hey, we had
some good times, though.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.300
Remember high school?

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.501
I used to hang out with you
and your friends.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.434
Watching you guys play hoops,

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:51.634
hoping you'd take a rake break.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:58.167
Who was that guy that used
to pour out half his Gatorade

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.501
then fill the empty half
with Yoo-Hoo

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.167
and call it Gator-Hoo?

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:08.000
Ed Zipperton.
Man, that guy was cool.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.267
He pantsed me at prom
while I was dancing alone

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.634
to "Lady in Red."

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.701
It was the part where it goes...

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.067
[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:21.000
♪ The lady in red ♪

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.767
-Yeah, it was.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:27.100
-♪ Is dancing with me ♪

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.200
♪ Cheek to cheek ♪

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.000
Then, shoop!

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.734
That's the sound
of my pants going down.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:38.601
And the worst part is, my pants
got caught on my prom boots.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:42.000
Yeah, the tuxedo rental man
at the mall tricked me

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.534
into paying extra for something
called prom boots.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:49.501
They were just Dr. Martens that
he spray-painted bright green.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.300
Oh, wait!
I forgot.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.601
I'm supposed to be doing
the voice of a rake.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:56.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.834
Not reciting
a page from my diary.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.567
-This has been another edition

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:04.334
of "Making James Read Lines
He's Never Seen Before."

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

